# ElizaOS's own PGlite store. 27 MB of database, machine-local, and regenerated on boot.
#
# It is also a TRAP worth naming: plugin-sql's `isReady()` is `!isShuttingDown()`, i.e.
# true for any live connection whether or not the schema exists. `AgentRuntime.initialize`
# only calls `adapter.init()` — which creates the core tables — when `isReady()` is false.
# So a first boot that dies after PGlite writes its cluster but before the schema lands
# leaves a database that is permanently "ready" and permanently empty, and every later run
# fails with `relation "agents" does not exist`. Deleting this directory is the fix.
.eliza/
